==Enemy==
Raging Bahamut Cat deals massive damage, enough to shred most units with under 320 range (including [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] and [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Sadako Cat]]), but has a long enough backswing to where a spam of meatshields like [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Cats]], [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Macho Cats]], [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cats]] and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall Cats]] can stall him quite effectively. [[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Jiangshi Cat]] is especially good at dealing with him considering he will always survive two hits from Raging Bahamut. He is definitely a priority to add since the previously mentioned meatshields will die to Bahamut instantly. To deal with him, it's best to keep a constant flow of meatshields, and spawn long-ranged attackers like [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cat]], [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] and [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]]. [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Surfer Cat]] will usually get killed before he can land a hit, but [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Psychocat]]'s 365 range makes him a very decent option against this enemy.

It goes without saying that the player should have all [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]] before fighting him. Even if they can stall him forever, his increased health may buy enough time for [[Alpacky]] to spawn.

